<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Griqualand East</h1><p class="st-meta">1862 CE – 1879 CE · capital Kokstad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The territory where Adam Kok III's Griqua resettled after their trek over the Drakensberg, with its capital at Kokstad.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After selling their land at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/philippolis-griqua-state">Philippolis</a> to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/orange-free-state">Orange Free State</a> in 1861, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adam-kok-iii">Adam Kok III</a> and some 2,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griqua">Griqua</a> trekked across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drakensberg">Drakensberg</a> with wagons and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, arriving in 1863 in Nomansland, a thinly settled area between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mpondo-kingdom">Mpondo Kingdom</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/natal-colony">Natal</a> that the Cape government had offered them.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griqua">Griqua</a> set up a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volksraad">Volksraad</a> under Kok and issued land titles to settlers. They founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokstad">Kokstad</a> in 1869 below Mount Currie. Many settlers, however, sold their farms to whites, and debt and land loss weakened the community.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> took over administration in 1874 and annexed the territory formally in 1879, after Kok's death in 1875 and a short <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griqua">Griqua</a> rising in 1878. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokstad">Kokstad</a> remains a centre of Griqua identity.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/griqualand-east.jpg" alt="Griqualand East" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Seb az86556 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FlagGriekwalandEast.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1862 CE – 1879 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kokstad</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Adam Kok III</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Cape Dutch, Khoekhoe</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nomansland, Adam Kok III's Griqualand</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1870&amp;focus=griqualand-east" aria-label="Griqualand East on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5443 3292 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Griqualand East lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5763 3548L5656 3538M5763 3548L5470 3663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5656 3538h0M5470 3663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5763 3548h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5763 3548h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kokstad. <a href="/atlas?year=1870&amp;focus=griqualand-east">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
